    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d168428b_752fb5d1",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaCallTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157922
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-20T01:48:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if disconnect here, may cause UI flash issue, when you make a emergency call, during the time, phone switch from UMTS to CDMA, the call will be ended, and UI will disappear, after get_current_call lists the call, notify as unknown call, UI appears again.\n\nin this case, lower layer must ensure the dial request is successful, so do not suggest disconnecting here, so that user has bad experience, the progress should be silent.",
      "parentUuid": "a247dd49_21c62474",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "e16fea2f3e1b4b266f56656b73ee330d04730be2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c699e368_55e7dba0",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaCallTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-20T17:23:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like a little bit of a bad or at the very least asymmetrical design to depend on the ECBM exit notification to indicate that we may be switching from CDMA to UMTS... Especially since there is no such indication for the other route from UMTS to CDMA.\n\nYou say \"phone switch from UMTS to CDMA, the call will be ended, and UI will disappear, after get_current_call lists the call, notify as unknown call, UI appears again\", but that doesn\u0027t appear to be the case. We had to place another dial() when trying to make a call and the phone switched from CDMA to UMTS, so why would we not have to redial when switching from UMTS to CDMA? Wouldn\u0027t the call just be dropped?",
      "parentUuid": "d168428b_752fb5d1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "e16fea2f3e1b4b266f56656b73ee330d04730be2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90c0f0eb_87158d7a",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaCallTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157922
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-21T03:24:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "in UMTS to CDMA case, the call request can be sent out successfully, modem acquires CDMA for emergency call under UMTS, so phone has to change as CMDA, because Modem ensures the emergency call successfully, in this case, even pending MO call is disposed, the unknown call will be notified, Telecom will take this case.\n\notherwise, the ecall may be sent out over IMS pipe, after handover to CS, then follow by handover case.\n\nin a word, the progress is silent if we did not disconnect the pending mo call.\n\nwe do not need to redial.\n\n\nin CDMA to UMTS case, after exiting ECBM, lower layer needs to take some times to acquire UMTS, unfortunately RIL sends the request with the preference CDMA_AUTOMATIC because lower layer does not report UMTS in time. because the voice call cannot be dialed out over CDMA, it is failed always, internally we have asked RIL to resolve this, but they think this is a hack, not follow by design.\n\nso Telephony has to make a change to delay the dial request.\n\n\nfor redial, if report generic error, Telecom can redial out over other SUB if it is emergency all. redial just is used for emergency call, of course, QC support redial based on emergency temp/perm failure for ecall also.\n\n\nhere the normal voice call is failed, so we make a 6s delay on this.",
      "parentUuid": "c699e368_55e7dba0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "e16fea2f3e1b4b266f56656b73ee330d04730be2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
